  "details": "<p>Local legend connects the site with the revolt of Boudica in AD 61. <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustus_Pitt-Rivers\" title=\"Augustus Pitt-Rivers\">Augustus Pitt-Rivers</a> first excavated the site in 1881.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ambresbury Banks is an archaeological site in the Epping Forest of Essex, England. It contains the remains of a 4.5 ha Iron Age hillfort on a site that is now forested.",
